# JAY-OS monorepo .gitignore
# Written BEFORE the first commit, deliberately -- see the repo's own
# history (or lack of it) for why that order matters: once a credential is
# committed, deleting it in a later commit does not remove it from history.

# --- Never committed, ever ---
secrets/
*.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
id_ed25519*
id_rsa*
*_token.json
google_token.json
google_client_secret.json
*credential*.json

# --- email-sentinel keeps its OWN separate git repo and remote ---
# (apps/email-sentinel/.git, pushed to JAY-OS-Email-Sentinel on GitHub).
# This monorepo does not absorb it: doing so would either destroy that
# repo's local history or create a broken nested-repo reference. Its files
# are gitignored here so `git add .` never tries to touch them.
apps/email-sentinel/

# --- Derived/regenerable data, not source ---
# The graph database and logs are rebuilt by `python -m graph ingest`; they
# are a local cache of Notion + the sentinel ledger, not something to diff
# or review in pull requests.
graph/jayos-graph.sqlite3
graph/jayos-graph.sqlite3-*
graph/pages/
graph/logs/
graph/vault-sample/
graph/graphify_compatible_export.json
/tmp/

# --- Generated permit PDFs (large binaries, one per permit, rebuilt from
# the .py build script sitting right next to them) ---
permits/*/*.pdf

# --- Demo/acceptance-test OUTPUT, not source. live_acceptance.py and
# live_canary.py (the scripts) are tracked; what running them produced is
# not. notion_outbox.json in particular carries a real Notion page id and a
# real teammate's Notion user id alongside its synthetic ZZ-TEST content --
# regenerable, and not something that belongs in git history either way. ---
orchestrator/permit_pipeline/demo/*.db
orchestrator/permit_pipeline/demo/notion_outbox.json

# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# --- Editor/OS noise ---
.DS_Store
*.swp

# --- Backup files left by earlier hand-edits ---
*.bak
*.bak-*
